From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:55:39 +0000
Subject: Match the start screen to the browser theme

Since Android 12 the system shows a start screen whenever the browser
starts without a running activity. It is drawn from the theme in the
manifest, which follows the system's dark mode: light by day and dark
gray at night. With AMOLED black on, the browser is black at night, so
that start screen does not match it.

On Android 13 and later, while AMOLED black is on, set the theme of the
next start screen to one that is light by day and black at night and
shows no icon, like the tabbed browser theme. With AMOLED black off,
reset it to the theme in the manifest.

The start screen keeps following the system's dark mode, not the
browser's Light or Dark setting. Android keeps one start screen theme
per app, so custom tabs and web apps started from the home screen use
it too, and custom tabs follow the system's dark mode unless the app
that opens them asks for a color scheme. A start screen taken from the
browser's setting would show a light screen before a dark custom tab,
or the reverse.

Android looks the theme up by name, so the name is kept in release
builds. The theme is set right after the AMOLED black switch is
written, and once per process in deferred startup, after the first
frame. Within a process it is set again only when it changes. Android
12 has no such setting and is unchanged.

